On Sun, 30 Jul 2023 10:02:08 +0530 Nilesh Patra <nilesh at debian.org> wrote:
> Package: r-bioc-rhdf5filters
> Version: 1.12.1+dfsg-2
> Severity: important
> 
> Dear Maintainer,
> 
> New version of rhdf5filters enables vbz and zstd compression as well but
> these have been ignored with a debian specific patch. As a result it
> enables only lz, blosc and bzip2.

I have pushed some changes to salsa to get this moving. However I
noticed that upstream itself has disabled vbz temporarily[1]. so it
makes sense to support this for us only when upstream does so as well.
So we should re-visit this in the next version.

For now, I reckon we are in a sensible state on this package (except
this has unused copies of vbz). I'm leaving the state of this package in
salsa as is (with my changes) for now.

[1]: https://github.com/grimbough/rhdf5filters/commit/e4b79ab2215d5c4e7298515cb28f79630585700c

Best,
Nilesh
